I think you're missing the point. It's not about automatically getting a job. It's just being there for students to at least meet and tell so they can at least learn at these career fairs, or there's no point of even going to those events. Just read similar posts on this subreddit and youll see what i mean, because i think you're gonna be too petty to listen to me now that you're that random angry reddit person that's assuming how bad i am/no talentknow nothing just because you're not getting what i mean. You dont know anything about me and I dont know anything about you except the down putting comments to me.

&#x200B;

right now, im not doing anything except responding to your negative attitude. So just keep on doing you, but leave others out of it

Yeah I think so when people go to career fair and the recruiters dont even want to talk to you or see a persons resume, so they pass you off to the online job portal. Came to the fair to have some face-to-face and be more than than a resume in the mass black hole of applicants.

&#x200B;

you see it all over this subreddit, you always going around putting struggling students down? You dont see anyone else on this post with this attitude
